     "e": "☀️🛝",
     "t": "{name} reads about Sara. One sunny day, Sara went to the park because she was bored."
    },
    {
     "e": "✏️🖼️",
     "t": "She drew a picture with her pencil. She was happy and smiled at her friend."
    },
    {
     "e": "🤕",
     "t": "Then she fell and hurt her knee. Sara felt sad and scared."
    },
    {
     "e": "🤝",
     "t": "Her friend helped her stand up."
    },
    {
     "e": "😊",
     "t": "Sara said, 'Thank you', and smiled again. Now she was tired, but she felt better."
    },
    {
     "e": "🔗",
     "t": "We use 'then' to tell what happens next, 'but' to show something different, and 'and' to add more."
    },
    {
     "e": "🐱🏙️",
     "t": "'c' is hard /k/ before a, o, u: cat, cold, cup. 'c' is soft /s/ before e, i, y: city, ice, face, pencil."
    }
